; expect 7
; A flat two-argument spine over a local holding a curried lambda
; chain: each indirect call absorbs exactly one argument and the
; result is the record for the next - `(h 3 4)` is "apply, then apply
; the result". Passing both arguments in one call answered with the
; inner closure's address; both compilers had that bug and both now
; chain.
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((h (lambda (a) (lambda (b) (+ a b)))))
    (h 3 4)))
